  "root_cause": "The 22 sub-floor members are ALL rung half-segments (member_id ('rung', i, seg_idx) for interior stations i=1..11, seg_idx in {0,1}). Under the model's own symmetric-vertical-load service case (equal downward Fz applied directly at every rail deck node, i.e. at the SAME nodes that are the rung half-segments' own endpoints), the primary vertical load path is NOT through the rungs at all: each rail deck node also connects via TWO eccentric 'link' bearing elements to the ends of the adjacent longitudinal rail members (the same +/-ecc/2 over/under notch idiom used at every interior joint), and it is THIS eccentric bearing offset that gives the longitudinal rails the moment arm needed to carry vertical load in arch/bending action -- exactly as in the plain 2-rail davinci_bridge. The transverse rung member at that same node is oriented purely in the y (transverse) direction and, under a load applied only in z at its own endpoints with the far endpoint free to move to equilibrium, requires essentially ZERO relative transverse-axis engagement to satisfy compatibility -- there is no y-direction (transverse) load, and no applied load anywhere in the model has a transverse component, so nothing forces a genuine axial/bending state into a member whose own axis IS the transverse direction. It is a real, reproducible modelling artifact of the 3-rail split-rung construction (each rung was split at the centre rail into two INDEPENDENT half-members purely to raise member-size diversity, at build time -- see the generator's own docstring: 'the single 2-rail rung member is naturally split by the added centre rail'), NOT a sizing/section-catalog artifact (confirmed: the same 22 members are below floor at every lambda/section combination tested in nonsingular_class_verification.json) and NOT specific to the service load case -- the self-weight-only case shows the exact same 22 members near-zero (see selfweight_se_J/selfweight_share_pct per member above), confirming the defect is topological (no path engages the rungs under ANY purely-vertical nodal loading), not an artifact of the specific -5500 N/node magnitude used in the campaigns."
}